{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 13 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". Count sequences with no run of 3 same bits. Classic combinatorics: number of binary strings of length n with no 3 consecutive equal bits. This is Fibonacci-like. Let's compute recurrence: Let a_n be number of strings length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit? Actually we can use states: last two bits? We need to avoid 3 consecutive same. Equivalent to sequences over alphabet {0,1} with no 3 consecutive same. This is like counting sequences with no 3 consecutive identical. We can use recurrence: Let A_n be number of valid strings length n. We can compute via DP with states representing last two bits or run length.\n\nDefine dp[n][k][b] where k=run length of last bit (1 or 2) and b=bit value. But easier: Let f[n][0] = number of strings length n ending with a single 0 (i.e., last run length 1). f[n][1] = ending with two consecutive 0s (run length 2). Similarly g[n][0] for ending with single 1, g[n][1] for ending with two 1s. But we can combine symmetrical: f for 0, g for 1. Recurrence: For n=1: f[1][0]=1 (string \"0\"), g[1][0]=1 (\"1\"). f[1][1]=0, g[1][1]=0.\n\nFor n>1: To get f[n][0] (ending with single 0), previous bit must be 1. So sum of all strings of length n-1 ending with 1 (either run length 1 or 2). So f[n][0] = g[n-1][0] + g[n-1][1].\n\nSimilarly g[n][0] = f[n-1][0] + f[n-1][1].\n\nFor f[n][1] (ending with two 0s), previous must be single 0. So f[n][1] = f[n-1][0].\n\nSimilarly g[n][1] = g[n-1][0].\n\nTotal A_n = f[n][0]+f[n][1]+g[n][0]+g[n][1].\n\nWe can compute up to n=13.\n\nLet's compute iteratively.\n\nInitialize n=1:\nf0=1, f1=0, g0=1, g1=0. Total=2.\n\nn=2:\nf0 = g0+g1 =1+0=1\ng0 = f0+f1 =1+0=1\nf1 = f0_prev =1\ng1 = g0_prev =1\nNow totals: f0=1,f1=1,g0=1,g1=1 => total=4.\n\nn=3:\nf0 = g0+g1 =1+1=2\ng0 = f0+f1 =1+1=2\nf1 = f0_prev =1\ng1 = g0_prev =1\nTotal= f0+f1+g0+g1 =2+1+2+1=6.\n\nn=4:\nf0 = g0+g1 =2+1=3\ng0 = f0+f1 =2+1=3\nf1 = f0_prev =2\ng1 = g0_prev =2\nTotal=3+2+3+2=10.\n\nn=5:\nf0 = g0+g1 =3"}}],"created":1790947208,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4879,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-4LGzGWHYia0Qpr9ayyRUkNxwbuZNrnRT","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4111,"prompt_ms":489.899,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.11916784237411822,"prompt_per_second":8391.525600174731,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2391.768,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.118341590612777,"predicted_per_second":320.6832769733519}}